No test was changed to make it pass. Two things were **added**: the object-code tools above, and `make_inventory.py`. The existing `static_checks.sh` was not edited in this pass; it cannot see the H1 defect because it works on source text (see section 8, item 3).

Why the host tests and mutation testing missed H1: they compile the source for x86 with a mock `memcpy`-free platform and judge behavior, not the AArch64 object code. A `memcpy` in a hold changes neither a result nor a counter. Only the disassembly shows it.

