## 11. Risks

- The board has never run this code. The host tests prove logic, not timing, memory attributes, or the behavior of the Linux TEE driver on error returns (V14).
- Object-code properties (like H1) are only caught by inspecting the AArch64 build; a compiler or flag change can reintroduce them. The new tools exist but are not yet part of `static_checks.sh`.
- The call graph has unresolved indirect calls (console and `kprintf`) and a panic path that reaches `trace_printf`; both are accepted limits, not proofs of absence.
- Rollback depends on one laptop disk and one working card; a disk failure loses every restore point.
- The prototype keys are readable by anyone with the tree; Normal World can read Secure World memory on this board.

