**Static checks and the new guard:** `static_checks.sh` gained an object-code section that runs `hold_memcpy_check.py` and `h1_objcheck.py` when `ON_DIS=<disassembly of the Monitor-ON tee.elf>` is set; without it, it prints `SKIPPED` rather than pretending. The previous version is in `source_snapshots/optee_os_20261107_h1fix_pre/static_checks.sh`.

**What is still not claimed:** the microsecond effect of removing the call from the hold (never measured), and anything about the board.

**Outstanding after this pass** (unchanged except H1): the 86 later interface checks are not mapped to evidence; the full SD image with the monitor enabled has not been built; the nine on-board checks, hold-time measurement and production key provisioning remain future activities that need your separate approval.
